  "disagreement": "Sanity check \u2014 the probes do not spuriously co-fire. Framed as chance-corrected *agreement* on the binary 'flagged unfaithful?' decision, the mean off-diagonal Cohen's kappa is \u2248 0.25 (0 = chance), i.e. the probes agree no more than chance off their shared corners (the raw Spearman \u2248 0.25 says the same but is population-composition-dependent, so we do not lead with it). The substantive point is qualitative and robust: the 'sycophant' model fails Silent-Hint-Injection (SHI faithfulness 0.00) yet passes Simulatability (SIM 1.00) and Step-Corruption (CSC 1.00) \u2014 any single probe used alone would have cleared it. That is why the unit of measurement is a card, not a scalar.",
